# Mandatory Engineering System Rule

This repository follows the Data Relay Labs Engineering System.

Before planning, editing, refactoring, fixing, testing, or releasing code:

1. Read @AGENTS.md.
2. Read @.engineering/project.yaml.
3. Read @.engineering/tests.yaml.
4. For release/version/artifact work, read @.engineering/release.yaml.
5. Use the Engineering System version/baseline declared by the project profile.
6. Identify the change class and affected domains before implementation.
7. Inspect relevant existing implementation and tests.
8. Make the smallest correct change; do not expand scope or perform unrelated refactors.
9. Run affected tests first, then wider gates required by risk/release policy.
10. A bug fix must add or identify durable regression coverage whenever practical.
11. Never weaken a valid test merely to obtain PASS.
12. Never report unexecuted, skipped, blocked, or historical evidence as current PASS.
13. Never reuse release qualification evidence from another source HEAD.
14. If mandatory engineering context is missing or contradictory, stop implementation and report the configuration problem instead of guessing.

Repository-local public contracts and release rules override generic assumptions. The canonical shared system is datarelay-labs/engineering-system.
